by stof at 2025-09-15T13:18:44Z

> > As far as the workflow component is concerned, the list of places and transitions is not a closed list (and so is a bad fit for an enum).
>
> Is it not the opposite of what @alexandre-daubois is saying? ("The consensus was that places are finite and precisely defined in the configuration, making them already "strongly typed"")

The list is finite for a given workflow instance in your project. The list of places is not finite in the workflow component, as it allows projects to configure the list of places. This means that the code in the component cannot benefit from type safety by using an enum as parameter type. Your own code could benefit from it in a `setStatus` method (or whatever the name).
This is why the marking store is the most important part of this support (configuration shortcuts are indeed just syntactic sugar for PHP config files, even though they provide a lot more values in declarative formats like Yaml).
